chmmc-cmm-2026-individual-12.body:
Let state $[n]$ mean two people share a number and the third differs from it by $n$ (the start is $[0]$). Let $a_n$ be the expected remaining time. Working out the $8$ coin outcomes:
* from $[0]$: $\frac34\to[1]$, $\frac14\to[0]$;
* from $[1]$: $\frac18\to[0]$, $\frac12\to[1]$, $\frac18\to[2]$, $\frac14$ stop;
* from $[n]$, $n\ge2$: $\frac18\to[n-1]$, $\frac14\to[n]$, $\frac18\to[n+1]$, $\frac12$ stop.
(The expected time is finite and bounded in $n$: from any state the process stops within two hours with probability at least $\frac3{16}$.)
